00:07:44.080 --> 00:07:45.920
 So, the data and graphics department,

00:07:45.920 --> 00:07:48.400
 its mission, as best as I can articulate it,

00:07:48.400 --> 00:07:51.680
 is for us to create digital journalism

00:07:51.680 --> 00:07:54.360
 that's important to the readers of the LA Times,

00:07:54.360 --> 00:07:55.720
 both in what they want to read

00:07:55.720 --> 00:07:58.120
 and what they ought to read, right?

00:07:58.120 --> 00:08:01.440
 With using data development and design.

00:08:01.440 --> 00:08:02.360
 And by development,

00:08:02.360 --> 00:08:05.520
 I mean actual computer code development, right?

00:08:05.520 --> 00:08:08.840
 So the people that are on this team, if you hit the next slide,

00:08:08.840 --> 00:08:12.240
 are not just reporters and editors and journalists

00:08:12.240 --> 00:08:15.160
 and people like me who went to journalism school.

00:08:15.160 --> 00:08:17.120
 They're also at the same time,

00:08:17.120 --> 00:08:20.440
 computer programmers, data analysts,

00:08:20.440 --> 00:08:23.000
 information designers, data scientists,

00:08:23.000 --> 00:08:25.960
 whatever you want to call it, they're nerds, right?

00:08:25.960 --> 00:08:30.040
 And so, we're kind of one of the more multi-hyphened teams

00:08:30.040 --> 00:08:32.240
 at the LA Times and that people are called upon

00:08:32.240 --> 00:08:35.040
 to not just do the traditional skills of journalism,

00:08:35.040 --> 00:08:38.280
 but also to have these technical skills

00:08:38.280 --> 00:08:42.240
 that let them find and tell stories in other ways.

00:08:42.240 --> 00:08:44.480
 And this is something that's increasingly common

00:08:44.480 --> 00:08:46.120
 across the journalism industry.

00:08:46.120 --> 00:08:48.400
 Our team is not unique.

00:08:48.400 --> 00:08:50.280
 There's kind of an evolution happening

00:08:50.280 --> 00:08:53.280
 in graphics and data departments across the country

00:08:53.280 --> 00:08:58.280
 where graphics is becoming kind of a higher-skill

00:09:00.520 --> 00:09:02.240
 data and programming profession.

00:09:02.240 --> 00:09:05.320
 And our team is caught in the same currents

00:09:05.320 --> 00:09:06.760
 that are driving that, right?

00:09:06.760 --> 00:09:10.760
